  "title": "Kourovka problem 20.115 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let χ be a complex irreducible character of a finite group G. If χ(x) ̸= 0 for\nsome x ∈ G, must the order o(x) of x divide |G|/χ(1)?\n   This is known to be true if G is solvable, and it is known that (o(x)χ(1))4 divides\n|G| for arbitrary G.                                                         T. Wilde",
